@startuml uc-pat-01-comm-alt-a4
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

title UC-PAT-01: Manage My Appointments (C5 v1.1.0)\nCommunication Diagram - Alternative Flow A4: Cancellation of an Urgent/Stat or Preferential Examination

actor ":Patient" as pat
boundary ":MyAppointmentsUI" as ui
control ":PatientAppointmentController" as ctrl
control ":PatientAppointmentService" as srv
entity ":Booking" as booking
control ":AuditService (C1)" as audit
control ":PendingOrderGateway (C4)" as c4
control ":BookingEventPublisher" as ev

pat -- ui : 1: chooseCancel()\n3: acknowledgeWarningAndConfirm(reason) >\n< 2: showClinicalPriorityWarning(priority, serviceContact)\n< 8: displayCancellation(CANCELLED)

ui -- ctrl : 4: POST my-appointments/{bookingId}/cancel\n(reason, priorityWarningAcknowledged = true, expectedBookingVersion) >\n< 7: HTTP 200 (AppointmentDetailsDTO, CANCELLED)

ctrl -- srv : 5: cancelAppointment(CancelAppointmentRequestDTO) >\n< 6: AppointmentDetailsDTO

srv -- booking : 5.1: [checks of A3 pass] cancel(reason, actorId, now) >

srv -- audit : 5.2: recordEvent(APPOINTMENT_CANCELLED, priority, warning acknowledged) >

srv -- c4 : 5.3: markOrderPending(orderId) >

srv -- ev : 5.4: publish(BookingChangedEvent CANCELLED) >

note bottom of ui
  2: the UI knows the priority from the details (step 6):
  STAT_URGENT or PREFERENTIAL -> warning and "contact the service".
  If the patient does not proceed, nothing is sent.
end note

note bottom of c4
  The ordering physician sees the order back in
  PENDING_SCHEDULING and the cancellation event
  in the order status (UC-PHY-03, It3).
  The other steps of A3 (slot, worklist, notification)
  are the same and are not repeated here.
end note
@enduml
